<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  WildAnimals_TheForge.xml                   UtinniPatches — new file
  ============================================================================
  THEFORGE_RM_MOD_BUILD_1. Wires the campaign's Star Wars fauna onto
  RM_TheForge's wildAnimals, layered on top of the 5 non-Star-Wars/from-
  scratch rows that mod ships inline (AA_Aerofleet, LavaSnail, AA_Metallovore,
  AA_CrescendoAnole, RM_FleetFlier). Per §7 Q11 ("RimMandrake should not name
  star wars ever"), RM_TheForge may not carry any Star Wars creature by any
  route, so every Star Wars row the frozen RUT_TheForge.xml carries rides
  HERE instead. Shape: WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml / WildAnimals_LeaningScrub.xml.

  🔑 SOURCE OF TRUTH: defNames and weights copied verbatim from the LIVE
  RUT_TheForge.xml wildAnimals block (read directly, not from
  rosters/the_forge.json, which THEFORGE_RM_MOD_BUILD_1's own analysis
  already found stale/incomplete against the live def).

  🔴 Two rows cast their OWNED RSW_ port, not the donor's bare defName —
  fixing a live mismatch, not merely following convention:
    - LavaFlea (mlie.starwarsanimalcollection, 0.25) -> cast as RSW_LavaFlea
    - Beldon (mlie.starwarsanimalcollection, 0.08) -> cast as RSW_Beldon.
      FORGE_MECHANICS_1's own tibanna-tap patch
      (Patches/RUT_TibannaTap_BeldonWiring.xml) has ALWAYS targeted
      RSW_Beldon, a defName that has never actually spawned on the frozen
      RUT_TheForge (whose own wildAnimals lists only the donor's bare
      Beldon). This op is the first place the tap's real target actually
      lives in a Forge wildAnimals list.
  RSW_Maguana (mandrake.rsw.swbestiary, 0.5) is already RSW_-tier and just
  needs the file - unchanged.

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing (PatchOperationConditional
  returns true on no match) - validated with
  skills/rimworld-modding/scripts/validate_patch.py against the live def
  dump and the full active mod set; an unmatched PatchOperationAdd is
  silent, so a clean run there is not proof a row landed.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_TheForge"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_TheForge"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <RSW_LavaFlea MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.25</RSW_LavaFlea>
        <RSW_Beldon MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.08</RSW_Beldon>
        <RSW_Maguana MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.5</RSW_Maguana>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
